model {
  extend basalt.modelGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Every fleet lane failure says where it happened in closed values only. Each read and send of configure and disable carries one closed step name (inspect, primary_read, settings_read, application_read, send, inspect_after, digest) beside the error's class, and a refused handoff answer prints its HTTP status as a number, so an answer the bridge made reads apart from one the Worker made. Configure re-reads the controller, sending nothing, for up to the controller's 300 s code handover: a read that throws or bindings that still lag the Worker settings wait, a typed refusal stands at once, and past the bound a throw refuses as controller-not-ready and lagging bindings as controller-bindings-differ, so no release order has to know the timing."
      constraint "The Worker's handoff entry writes one closed POOL_RUNTIME_COMMAND_REFUSED line, with its status, for every answer but a 200: a 409 refusal, a 500 defect and the early 405 and 413 alike. Writing the line never changes the answer."
      constraint "A health read that ended by nothing but its own caller's abort, such as the guard's probe at its deadline, writes no POOL_RUNTIME_ENDPOINT_FAILURE: the guard keeps its own outcome and elapsed time. A send that failed before the abort, and every other aborted call, still writes one."
      constraint "POOL_FLEET_GROWTH_REFUSED carries a provider refusal's closed code beside its class, as the pending-pass lines do, through one shared helper."
      constraint "Recovery keeps how the primary it restarts had ended as that boot's own end: each round records it before admitting a restart and only when none is kept for that boot, so a restart attempt that ends before it serves never replaces it, and the record changes only when a later boot ends in its turn."
      constraint "The controller keeps one record of the selected root's last recovery in closed values: the boot it restarts, when it was detected, when the root served again, its rounds, and the latest eight rounds' refusals. A served root's next recovery starts a new record. Healthy passes read it once per isolate and write only to end an open recovery, its writes never change what a round does, and the controller inspect returns it for the lane to print keyed by the restarted boot's short hash."
    }
  }
}
